        <mxCell id="g1" value="inspection report" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ft2" target="pr1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g2" value="submitted report" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr1" target="d1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g3" value="received report" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr1" target="pr2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g4" value="validation note" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr2" target="ft2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="670" y="340" /><mxPoint x="135" y="340" /></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g5" value="accepted report" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr2" target="pr3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g6" value="routing entry" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="d2" target="pr3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g7" value="report with resolved destination" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr3" target="pr4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g8" value="delivery record" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr4" target="d1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g9" value="work item" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr4" target="el2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g10" value="work item" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr4" target="dr2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g11" value="work item" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="pr4" target="st2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="n3" value="OBSERVED IN THE DELIVERY LOG (W06-S04)&#10;The log records work items received by Electrical and Drainage only. No work item in this export was received by Structures. The flow to Structures is shown because W06-S01 places all three departments inside the receiving boundary; the discrepancy is reported on page 3, not corrected here." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1430" y="760" width="430" height="180" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n4" value="A rejected report does not continue to routing (W06-S01). Routing-table maintenance by the service administrator is outside this boundary." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="760" width="380" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram name="3 Data Definitions and Finding" id="p3">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="800" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="900" pageHeight="1500" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="h3" value="Page 3 &#8212; Data Definitions and Finding" style="text;html=1;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="25" width="800" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="h3b" value="Curtis Loop &#183; CIT 140 Week 6 &#183; Inspection Report Routing System" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#555555;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="52" width="800" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="b1" value="1. Data definitions &#8212; inspection report (field contract, W06-S02)&#10;&#10;report_id        Unique report reference; CJ- followed by three digits.&#10;asset_id         Reference for the inspected asset; two-letter prefix and three digits.&#10;asset_type       One of STREETLIGHT, DRAIN or BRIDGE.&#10;finding_code     One of LAMP_OUT, BLOCKED or SURFACE_DAMAGE.&#10;priority         One of ROUTINE or URGENT; urgency does not change the department.&#10;captured_at      UTC capture time, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ.&#10;photo_ref        Attachment reference, IMG- followed by three digits.&#10;survey_area      One of NORTH, CENTRAL or SOUTH.&#10;&#10;All eight fields are required. Process 2 checks the report against this contract." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="85" width="820" height="250" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="b2" value="2. Data stores&#10;&#10;D1  Report Register   Submitted reports written by process 1 and delivery records written by process 4.&#10;                      The delivery log in W06-S04 is an export from this store.&#10;D2  Routing Table     Routing entries read by process 3 to resolve a destination.&#10;                      Maintained by a service administrator outside the modeled boundary." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="350" width="820" height="140" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="b3" value="3. Required destination policy (W06-S03)&#10;&#10;STREETLIGHT  &#8594;  Electrical          DRAIN  &#8594;  Drainage          BRIDGE  &#8594;  Structures&#10;&#10;ROUTINE and URGENT set urgency within the receiving department. They do not change the department." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="505" width="820" height="110" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="b4" value="4. Required against observed (W06-S02, W06-S03, W06-S04)&#10;&#10;report_id   asset_type     required      received by    result&#10;CJ-601      STREETLIGHT    Electrical    Electrical     match&#10;CJ-602      DRAIN          Drainage      Drainage       match&#10;CJ-603      BRIDGE         Structures    Electrical     DISCREPANCY&#10;CJ-604      BRIDGE         Structures    Electrical     DISCREPANCY&#10;CJ-605      STREETLIGHT    Electrical    Electrical     match&#10;CJ-606      DRAIN          Drainage      Drainage       match&#10;CJ-607      BRIDGE         Structures    Electrical     DISCREPANCY&#10;CJ-608      STREETLIGHT    Electrical    Electrical     match&#10;&#10;5 of 8 delivered to the required department. All three BRIDGE reports went to Electrical.&#10;Structures received no work item in this export." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="630" width="820" height="290" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="b5" value="5. Finding&#10;&#10;Every report in the export was validated as ACCEPTED, so the field contract check in process 2 is not the point of failure. The discrepancy appears after validation, at the point where process 3 resolves a destination: all three BRIDGE reports were delivered to Electrical instead of Structures, while STREETLIGHT and DRAIN reports reached their required departments.&#10;&#10;The pattern is consistent rather than intermittent, and it tracks asset_type alone. It is not explained by priority, since CJ-604 was URGENT and CJ-603 and CJ-607 were ROUTINE and all three were routed the same way, and W06-S03 states urgency does not change the department. It is not explained by survey_area, since the three affected reports came from CENTRAL, NORTH and SOUTH.&#10;&#10;Effect on the receiving departments: Structures received no inspection work from this export, including a BRIDGE report marked URGENT, while Electrical received three work items outside its remit." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="935" width="820" height="290" as="geometry" /></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="b6" value="6. What the records do not establish&#10;&#10;The cause of the discrepancy is not established by the supplied evidence. W06-S03 describes the required destination but does not prove what entries the running Routing Table contained, and no runtime table snapshot, deployment history or code was supplied. W06-S04 states that a routing discrepancy is evidence of a result and that its technical cause remains a question until supporting evidence is obtained.&#10;&#10;Open questions for the next step: what entry, if any, D2 Routing Table holds for BRIDGE; when that entry was last changed and by whom, which falls to the service administrator outside this boundary; and whether any earlier export shows BRIDGE reports reaching Structures. This finding reports the discrepancy and does not record a repair." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1240" width="820" height="225" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

</mxfile>
